{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589696142,"sessionID":"ses_e2a1ee82bffezgZpHiX4XWVTsI","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5e19aae001U8dUq3rRcMAlND","sessionID":"ses_e2a1ee82bffezgZpHiX4XWVTsI","messageID":"msg_1d5e1818f0016z8OOhPdVh4KOw","type":"tool","id":"call_7b7c312ff4c34632ba161e96","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"score-command-transcripts\\.mjs|narrows either mode|row-id","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md"},"output":"Found 3 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:\n  Line 112: | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n\n  Line 114: | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n\n  Line 154: node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs \\\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":3,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 3 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:\n  Line 112: | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude tu